WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
ORBITIQ is an independent engineering prototype exploring how AI can help manage satellite-to-cellular connectivity.

00:05.000 --> 00:13.000
ORBITIQ starts with publicly available cellular infrastructure data rather than fabricated topology. [REAL: OpenCelliD]

00:13.000 --> 00:21.000
It combines this with public orbital data to determine satellite visibility and candidate paths. [REAL: CelesTrak, SGP4]

00:21.000 --> 00:29.000
The digital twin then models thousands of mobile devices and network conditions. [SIMULATED: 10,000+ devices]

00:29.000 --> 00:39.000
When a satellite becomes congested, the system detects abnormal behavior. Utilization 72 to 94 percent, latency 42 to 89 milliseconds.

00:39.000 --> 00:47.000
Machine-learning models predict which users are likely to experience degraded connectivity within five minutes.

00:47.000 --> 00:57.000
The optimization engine ranks alternative satellite paths and explains why a handoff is recommended.

00:57.000 --> 01:05.000
Engineers can simulate an outage and compare network behavior before and after the AI recommendation.

01:05.000 --> 01:15.000
A grounded AI copilot lets engineers investigate incidents using telemetry and model results — never invented data.

01:15.000 --> 01:22.000
Real data, AI/ML, digital twin, network optimization, GenAI. ORBITIQ — independent research, no proprietary SpaceX data used.
